          "id": "ca1658dfd2f687d41cddda7556a8dd23eed1d431",
          "message": "add `parallelism` and `python` functionality to partitions (#149)\n\nSUMMARY:\r\n* add functionality for `python` version selection\r\n* add support for specifying `parallelism`. when using the `parallelism`\r\nkey, partitions will be generated with `pytest` commands that leverage\r\nshard functionality. please see pytest documentation\r\n[here](https://pypi.org/project/pytest-shard/) for more details.\r\n\r\nNOTES: consider the following example,\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n> cat neuralmagic/tests/partitions/nightly.yml\r\n# This file is loosely derived from \".buildkite/test-pipeline.yaml\"\r\n# It defines partitions for fan-out. Please keep the schema compatible\r\n# with \".buildkite/test-pipeline.yaml\". This means it is okay to add\r\n# Neural Magic specific keys, but do not remove or change ones that\r\n# are specifically from \"./buildkite/test-pipeline.yaml\"\r\n# or \"yaml\" files in directory \".buildkite\" generally.\r\n\r\nsteps:\r\n\r\n- label: Kernels\r\n  mirror_hardwares: [amd]\r\n  num_gpus: 1\r\n  gpu: l4\r\n  source_file_dependencies:\r\n  - csrc/\r\n  - vllm/attention\r\n  - tests/kernels\r\n  commands:\r\n    - pytest -v -s kernels --ignore=kernels/test_cutlass.py\r\n  parallelism: 2\r\n  python: 3.10.15\r\n```\r\n\r\nwill generate these partitions,\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n> cat partitions.json\r\n[\r\n  {\r\n    \"label\": \"gcp-k8s-l4-solo\",\r\n    \"python\": \"3.10.15\",\r\n    \"entry_label\": \"Kernels 0\",\r\n    \"commands\": [\r\n      \"pytest -v -s kernels --ignore=kernels/test_cutlass.py --shard-id=0 --num-shards=2\"\r\n    ]\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"label\": \"gcp-k8s-l4-solo\",\r\n    \"python\": \"3.10.15\",\r\n    \"entry_label\": \"Kernels 1\",\r\n    \"commands\": [\r\n      \"pytest -v -s kernels --ignore=kernels/test_cutlass.py --shard-id=1 --num-shards=2\"\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n]%                       \r\n```\r\n\r\nTEST PLAN:\r\nruns on remote push\r\n\r\n---------\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: andy-neuma <andy@neuralmagic.com>",
